      "target": {
        "verse": 10,
        "text": "And so I saw the wicked buried; they had come and gone from the holy place[a], and had boasted[b] in the city where they had done so. This too is vanity.[c]",
        "footnotes": [
          {
            "marker": "a",
            "text": "“The holy place” may refer to the temple precincts or another sacred place.",
            "reason": "cultural_note"
          },
          {
            "marker": "b",
            "text": "Unapplied alternative: a Hebrew bet reading reported in manuscript collations is interpreted here as “had boasted”; Greek and Latin instead express “were praised.” The Masoretic Hebrew and consulted Syriac and Targum texts express forgetting. The exact earliest wording, subject and timing remain uncertain.",
            "reason": "textual_variant"
          },
          {
            "marker": "c",
            "text": "Hebrew hebel, traditionally rendered “vanity”; it can also mean “vapor,” suggesting something fleeting or elusive.",
            "reason": "lexical_alternative"
          }
        ]
      }
